{"id":"longest-common-subsequence","title":"Longest common subsequence","difficulty":"medium","pattern":"two-sequence DP","statement":"<p>Return the length of the longest common subsequence of two strings.</p>","entry":{"python":"longest_common_subsequence","cpp":{"name":"longestCommonSubsequence","ret":"int","params":[["string","a"],["string","b"]]}},"kind":"function","compare":"exact","time_limit_ms":2000,"hints":["dp[i][j] = the LCS of the prefixes a[:i] and b[:j].","If the last characters match, extend dp[i\u22121][j\u22121]; otherwise drop one of them."],"complexity":"O(|a|\u00b7|b|) time, O(|b|) space","starter":{"python":"def longest_common_subsequence(a, b):\n    pass\n","cpp":"int longestCommonSubsequence(string a, string b) {\n    \n}\n"},"tests":[{"args":["abcde","ace"],"expected":3,"sample":true},{"args":["abc","abc"],"expected":3,"sample":true},{"args":["abc","def"],"expected":0},{"args":["a","a"],"expected":1},{"args":["",""],"expected":648},{"args":["",""],"expected":700}],"solution":{"explanation":"<p>The template for every two-sequence DP: the state is a pair of prefix lengths, and the transition looks at the last characters. Match: 1 + dp[i\u22121][j\u22121]. Otherwise: max(dp[i\u22121][j], dp[i][j\u22121]). Rolling rows cut memory to O(|b|). Reconstructing the subsequence needs the full table, or Hirschberg's divide and conquer.</p>","python":"def longest_common_subsequence(a, b):\n    prev = [0] * (len(b) + 1)\n    for x in a:\n        cur = [0]\n        for j, y in enumerate(b): cur.append(prev[j] + 1 if x == y else max(prev[j + 1], cur[j]))\n        prev = cur\n    return prev[-1]\n","cpp":"int longestCommonSubsequence(string a, string b) {\n    int m = b.size(); vector<int> prev(m + 1, 0), cur(m + 1, 0);\n    for (char x : a) { for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) cur[j + 1] = x == b[j] ? prev[j] + 1 : max(prev[j + 1], cur[j]); swap(prev, cur); }\n    return prev[m];\n}\n"}}